---
description: Follow the repository's operating contract for all work.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow `AGENTS.md` before making changes. It is the authoritative
repository contract for source locations, generated files, visual work,
verification, and operations.

For visual changes, also read `STYLE.md` before editing. Keep diffs small,
preserve unrelated working-tree changes, and do not hand-edit `dist/`.

On this Windows workspace, prefer `npm.cmd` when PowerShell blocks `npm.ps1`.
Before considering work complete, run `npm run verify` and `npm test`; run a
build when source assets or publish output may be affected. Do not run deploy
commands, change CI/CD, install dependencies, push, merge, or modify secrets
without explicit approval.

Treat `.env`, `.dev.vars`, and their variants as sensitive. Do not open,
expose, copy, or add their values to source control, prompts, logs, or output.
